    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104715" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρήχω</span></b> , wrongly assumed as pres. of
		Homeric pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέτρηχα,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταράσσω.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in later 
				Ep.
			, <i>to be rough</i> or <i>uneven,</i>
			pres.
			part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρήχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					72
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				521
			</span></i>: for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέτρηχα</span> in this sense, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταράσσω</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>.</div>
